===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[departure]].
#* {{RQ:Dunsany Pegana
|passage=Māna-Yood-Sushāī was before the beginning of the gods, and shall be after their '''going'''. […] After the '''going''' of the gods there will be no small worlds nor big.}}
#* {{RQ:Beckett Watt|text=But he found it strange to think {{...}} of all these little things that cluster round the comings, and the stayings, and the '''goings''', that he would know nothing of them, nothing of what they had been, as long as he lived, {{...}}}}
# The [[suitability]] of [[ground]] for riding, walking etc.
#: {{ux|en|The '''going''' was very difficult over the ice.}}
# [[progress|Progress]].
#: {{ux|en|We made good '''going''' for a while, but then we came to the price.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Conditions for advancing in any way.
#: {{ux|en|Not only were the streets not paved with gold, but the '''going''' was difficult for an immigrant.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} Course of life; behaviour; doings; ways.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Job|34|21|text=His eyes are upon the ways of man, and he seeth all his '''goings'''.}}
# {{lb|en|in the phrase "the going of"}} The [[whereabouts]] (of something).
#: {{ux|en|I can't find my sunglasses; you haven't seen the '''going''' of them, have you?}}
# The [[horizontal]] [[distance]] between the front of one [[step]] in a flight of stairs and the front of the next.
#: {{ux|en|Each step had a rise of 170 mm and a '''going''' of 250 mm.}}

